      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before Durand, the area was the Elton settlement founded in 1835, where families like the Pettengills and Felts first homesteaded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durand%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fires in 1886, 1904, and 1912 devastated Durand, leading Illinois to establish its first tax‑supported volunteer fire department in 1925.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/durand_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village celebrated a 2002 expansion of the Otter Creek subdivision, a modern effort to grow while preserving its historic character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/durand_illinois",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Durand’s community featured 17 houses, a post office named Tyler, general store, blacksmith, cooper shop, and a stage stop for travelers heading to Galena or Mineral Point.",
